","The entropy change (ΔS) for a reaction is calculated using the following formula:

ΔS = (nS_f(products)) - (nS_f(reactants))

where n is the molar coefficient of each substance in the balanced reaction and S_f is the standard molar entropy of the substance.

For the given reaction:

\[ 2 \text{PbS(s)} + 3 \text{O}_2(g) \rightarrow 2 \text{PbO(s)} + 2 \text{SO}_2(g) \]

We are given the molar entropies:

- S_f(PbS) = 91.2 J/K mol
- S_f(O_2) = 205.1 J/K mol
- S(PbO) = 66.5 J/K mol
- S_f(SO_2) = 248.2 J/K mol

Now, we can calculate the entropy change:

ΔS = 2 * S_f(PbO) + 2 * S_f(SO_2) - (2 * S_f(PbS) + 3 * S_f(O_2))

ΔS = (2 * 66.5) + (2 * 248.2) - (2 * 91.2 + 3 * 205.1)

ΔS = 133.0 + 496.4 - (182.4 + 615.3)

ΔS = 629.4 - 797.7

ΔS = -168.3 J/K mol

The entropy change for the reaction is -168.3 J/K mol.",relevance,"# Task Description
