What is the relationship used to estimate the flammability limits of mixtures from the data for individual fuels?<end_of_turn>
<start_of_turn>model
","The relationship used to estimate the flamen-

 efficiency of air-fuel mixtures is the ** Clausius-Raptine equation**, also known as the ** Clausian expansion**. This equation is given by:

\[
\frac{L}{L_{\text{gas}}} = \sum_{i=1}^{n} \frac{x_i}{1 + \frac{1}{1-2\phi} \left( \frac{1}{\phi} - 1 \right) \left( \frac{1 - \frac{1}{\phi}}{\phi} \right) \left( \frac{1 - \frac{1}{\phi}}{\phi} \right)}
\]

