To calculate the standard enthalpy change (ΔH°) for the reaction, we can use the following formula:

ΔH° = Σ ΔH°f(products) - Σ ΔH°f(reactants)

where ΔH°f is the standard enthalpy of formation.

For the given reaction:

ΔH° = [ΔH°f(Ca(OH)2(s))],
ΔH°f(H2O(l))] - [ΔH°f(CaO(s)) + ΔH°f(H2O(l)))

