ΔH° = (-986.2 kJ/mol) - (-635.1 kJ/mol)
ΔH° = -986.2 kJ/mol + 635.1 kJ/mol
ΔH° = -351.1 kJ/mol

The standard enthalpy change for the reaction between calcium oxide and water to form calcium hydrolyzed is -351.1 kJ/mol.
