","Let the sequence of vectors be $a_1, a_2, \ldots, a_n, \ldots$. We are given that $a_1 = (-2015, 14)$ and $a_n - a_{n-1} = (1, 1)$ for all $n \leq 2$. This means that the difference between consecutive terms is constant, so the sequence is an arithmetic sequence.

The general form of the sequence can be obtained as:
\[
a_n = a_1 + (n-1)(a_2 - a_1) = a_1 + (n-1)(1, 1) = (-2015, 14) + (n-1)(1, 1) = (-2015 + n - 1, 14 + n - 1) = (-2016 + n, 13 + n).
\]
The magnitude of $a_n$ is:
\[
