For $n = 1001$, $a_{1001} = (-2016 + 1001, 13 + 1001) = (-1015, 1014)$. Then $|a_{1001}| = \sqrt{(-1015)^2 + 1014^2} = \sqrt{1030225 + 1028196} = \sqrt{2058421} \approx 1434.6$.

For $n = 1002$, $a_{1002} = (-2016 + 1002, 13 + 1002) = (-1014, 1015)$. Then $|a_{1002}| = \sqrt{(-1014)^2 + 1015^2} = \sqrt{1028196 + 1030225} = \sqrt{2058421} \approx 1434.6$.

Thus, the smallest magnitude occurs at $n = 1001$ or $n = 1002$.

