486 divided by 3 is 162.
162 divided by 3 is 54.
54 divided by 3 is 18.
18 divided by 3 is 6.
6 divided by 3 is 2.

Thus, $1458 = 2 \cdot 3^6$. Thus, $g(1458) = g(2 \cdot 3^6) = 4^6 g(2)$.

Since $1 \leq 2 \leq 3$, we can use the given form of $g(x)$ to find $g(2)$:
$$ g(2) = 2 - 2|2 - 2| = 2 - 2(0) = 2. $$
Thus, $g(1458) = 4^6 g(2) = 4^6 \cdot 2 = 4096 \cdot 2 = 8192$.

